────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P1-01]  HOLD BILL AT POS
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : XS | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  At a busy counter, a cashier sometimes builds a bill for a customer who then
  steps away to check on something (price, item, partner approval). The cashier
  must serve the next customer immediately. Currently, leaving mid-bill loses all
  added items. The cashier is forced to make the next customer wait or lose all
  the work done on the first bill.

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As a CASHIER, I want to hold the current in-progress bill so I can serve the
  next customer without losing the items already added to the cart.

  As a CASHIER, I want to retrieve any held bill from a list and continue from
  where I left off.

  As a CASHIER, I want to delete a held bill if the customer does not return.

  WORKFLOW
  --------
  1. Cashier is building a bill — has 3 items in cart
  2. Customer says "wait, let me check" and steps aside
  3. Cashier clicks [Hold Bill] button on POS screen
  4. System saves the cart to a "held bills" local state with a label
     (e.g. "Hold #1 — 3 items — 11:42 AM")
  5. POS clears to an empty cart — cashier serves next customer normally
  6. When first customer returns, cashier clicks [Held Bills] panel
  7. Selects "Hold #1" — cart restores with all original items
  8. Cashier completes the sale normally

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - POS page: [Hold Bill] button added to cart header
  - POS page: [Held Bills] panel/drawer (slide-out list of held carts)
  - Each held bill shows: hold number, item count, subtotal, time held
  - [Resume] and [Delete] action per held bill

  DATABASE CHANGES
  ----------------
  No database change needed.
  Held bills are stored in-memory (React state or localStorage) only.
  They are NOT persisted — if the browser is refreshed, held bills are cleared.
  This is acceptable behaviour for a POS counter session.

  IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
  -------------------
  - Add `heldBills: CartItem[][]` state in POS component
  - [Hold Bill] button pushes current cart to heldBills array and clears cart
  - Held bills panel maps heldBills and shows [Resume] / [Discard] per hold
  - [Resume] restores the selected hold back to the active cart

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] Cashier can hold a bill with at least 1 item in the cart
  [ ] Held bill panel shows all currently held bills with item count and time
  [ ] Resuming a held bill restores exact items and quantities to the cart
  [ ] Multiple bills can be held simultaneously (at least 3)
  [ ] Discarding a held bill removes it from the list permanently
  [ ] POS receipt does not show any held bill reference — only completed sales


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P1-02]  AGED DEBTORS REPORT
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : S | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  The current system shows total credit outstanding per customer but cannot
  answer: "Which customers have owed money for more than 60 days?" This is one
  of the most critical financial reports for any trade business. Without it, the
  owner does not know who to chase for payment and overdue debts go unnoticed.

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As an OWNER, I want to see all outstanding customer balances grouped by how
  long they have been overdue, so I can prioritize collection calls.

  As an OWNER, I want to download the aged debtors report as a PDF to share with
  my accountant or to take to the bank.

  REPORT STRUCTURE
  ----------------
  Customer Name | Total Outstanding | 0-30 Days | 31-60 Days | 61-90 Days | 90+ Days

  Logic: For each credit sale, the "age" is calculated from the sale date to
  today. Partial payments reduce the oldest bucket first.

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - New report page: /reports/aged-debtors
  - Table: one row per customer with balance, grouped by age bucket
  - Summary row: totals per age bucket
  - Filter: show only customers with balance > 0
  - [Download PDF] button

  DATABASE CHANGES
  ----------------
  No new tables needed. Query joins:
    customers → sales (payment_type IN CREDIT, SPLIT, balance_amount > 0)
    customers → customer_payments (to subtract payments made)

  SQL APPROACH
  ------------
  SELECT customer, sale_date, balance_amount
  FROM sales
  WHERE payment_type IN ('CREDIT','SPLIT') AND balance_amount > 0
  Then in application layer, bucket by (TODAY - sale_date):
    0-30 days, 31-60, 61-90, 90+

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] Report shows only customers with outstanding credit balance > 0
  [ ] Each customer row shows total balance split into 4 age buckets
  [ ] Summary row at bottom shows total of each bucket column
  [ ] Clicking a customer row opens their account statement (links to P1-05)
  [ ] PDF download produces clean table with date generated and grand total
  [ ] OWNER and ADMIN roles can access; CASHIER and STORE_KEEPER cannot


