  - Bank loans (collateral valuation)
  - Annual accounting and tax filing
  - Understanding how much cash is locked in inventory

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As an OWNER, I want to see the current value of all my inventory at cost price,
  grouped by category, so I can understand how much capital is in my stock.

  As an OWNER, I want to download the stock valuation as a PDF for my accountant.

  REPORT STRUCTURE
  ----------------
  Category | Product Name | SKU | Unit | Stock Qty | Unit Cost | Total Value
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Fasteners & Fixings | Hex Bolt M6 | FF-001 | PCS | 450 | Rs.7 | Rs.3,150
  ...
  CATEGORY SUBTOTAL: Rs. XX,XXX
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  GRAND TOTAL STOCK VALUE: Rs. X,XXX,XXX

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - New report page: /reports/stock-valuation
  - Grouped by category (collapsible sections)
  - Filter: All / Active only / Low stock only / By category
  - Sort: By value (highest first) or alphabetical
  - [Download PDF] button

  DATABASE CHANGES
  ----------------
  No new tables. Query:
