────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P1-06]  PURCHASE ORDER (PO)
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : L | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  Currently the system only records stock AFTER it arrives (GRN). Real business
  requires raising a formal Purchase Order first — before goods are dispatched
  by the supplier. Without PO, there is no record of what was ordered, no way to
  follow up on pending deliveries, and no way to verify that what arrived matches
  what was ordered.

  WORKFLOW
  --------
  RAISE PO  →  SEND TO SUPPLIER  →  GOODS ARRIVE  →  RECEIVE (GRN against PO)
  [DRAFT]       [SENT/PENDING]        [PARTIAL / FULL]    [CLOSED]

  PO STATUSES:
    DRAFT     — being prepared, not yet sent to supplier
    SENT      — sent to supplier, awaiting delivery
    PARTIAL   — some items received, rest still pending
    RECEIVED  — all items received (GRN created), PO closed
    CANCELLED — PO cancelled before delivery

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As an OWNER/STORE_KEEPER, I want to create a Purchase Order to a supplier
  listing the products I need and the quantities, so the supplier knows exactly
  what to send.

  As a STORE_KEEPER, when stock arrives, I want to create a GRN against an
  existing PO so I can verify received quantities match ordered quantities.

  As an OWNER, I want to see all open POs (sent but not yet received) so I can
  follow up on pending deliveries.

  DATABASE TABLES NEEDED
  ----------------------
  purchase_orders:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    supplier_id     BIGINT REFERENCES suppliers(id)
    po_number       TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE
    status          TEXT CHECK (IN 'DRAFT','SENT','PARTIAL','RECEIVED','CANCELLED')
    expected_date   DATE
    notes           TEXT
    created_by      UUID REFERENCES users(id)
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()

  purchase_order_items:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    po_id           BIGINT REFERENCES purchase_orders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
    product_id      BIGINT REFERENCES products(id)
    ordered_qty     NUMERIC(10,3) NOT NULL
    received_qty    NUMERIC(10,3) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
    unit_price      NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - /purchase-orders            — list of all POs with status filter
  - /purchase-orders/new        — create PO form (supplier + items)
  - /purchase-orders/[id]       — PO detail with status, items, history
  - /purchase-orders/[id]/receive — receive goods form (enter received qty per item)
  - PDF: Purchase Order document (to send/print for supplier)

  LINK TO EXISTING GRN
  --------------------
  When receiving against a PO, a GRN (purchases record) is auto-created.
  The existing purchases table gets a po_id foreign key:
    ALTER TABLE purchases ADD COLUMN po_id BIGINT REFERENCES purchase_orders(id);

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] PO can be created with multiple products and quantities
  [ ] PO PDF can be downloaded and sent to supplier
  [ ] PO status changes correctly through its lifecycle
  [ ] When receiving goods, system compares received qty vs ordered qty
  [ ] Short deliveries are flagged (received < ordered)
  [ ] GRN is auto-created when goods are received against a PO
  [ ] Dashboard shows count of open (SENT) POs
  [ ] OWNER and STORE_KEEPER can create POs; CASHIER cannot


