────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P1-08]  PROFIT & LOSS REPORT
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : M | Dependency : P1-07 (Expense Tracking)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  The single most important financial report for any business owner. Currently
  the system shows revenue and purchase cost separately — but never combines them
  into a meaningful P&L. The owner does not know if the business is actually
  profitable.

  P&L STRUCTURE
  -------------
  REVENUE
    Total Sales Revenue                       Rs. X,XXX,XXX
    Less: Returns & Refunds                   Rs.    XX,XXX
    NET REVENUE                               Rs. X,XXX,XXX

  COST OF GOODS SOLD (COGS)
    Total Purchase Cost of Items Sold         Rs.   XXX,XXX
    GROSS PROFIT                              Rs.   XXX,XXX
    Gross Margin %                                      XX%

  OPERATING EXPENSES
    Rent & Utilities                          Rs.    XX,XXX
    Staff & Labour                            Rs.    XX,XXX
    Transport & Vehicle                       Rs.    XX,XXX
    Bank & Finance                            Rs.     X,XXX
    Other Expenses                            Rs.     X,XXX
    TOTAL EXPENSES                            Rs.   XXX,XXX

  NET PROFIT / (LOSS)                         Rs.   XXX,XXX
  Net Margin %                                           XX%

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - /reports/profit-loss
  - Date range selector (month, quarter, custom)
  - Visual chart: Revenue vs COGS vs Expenses vs Net Profit (bar chart)
  - [Download PDF] button

  COGS CALCULATION NOTE
  ---------------------
  COGS = Sum of (quantity_sold × buying_price) for each sale_item in period.
  This requires joining sale_items → products to get buying_price at time of sale.
  Ideally: store buying_price on sale_items at the time of sale (snapshot pricing).
  Current schema does not store this — may need migration to add buying_price to
  sale_items table.

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] P&L shows correct Revenue, COGS, Gross Profit for selected period
  [ ] Expenses from expense_categories are grouped and totalled
  [ ] Net Profit = Gross Profit - Total Expenses
  [ ] Gross Margin % and Net Margin % calculated correctly
  [ ] PDF download includes period, date generated, all line items
  [ ] OWNER and ADMIN access only


