  [P1-09]  QUOTATION / ESTIMATE GENERATION
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : L | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  Hardware shops frequently receive requests from contractors and construction
  companies to quote on a list of materials before committing to a purchase.
  Currently staff write quotes on paper, items get lost, and there is no way to
  convert an approved quote to a sale. This causes lost revenue and wasted time.

  WORKFLOW
  --------
  CREATE QUOTE → SEND TO CUSTOMER → CUSTOMER APPROVES → CONVERT TO SALE
  [DRAFT]          [SENT]              [ACCEPTED]            [INVOICED]

  QUOTE STATUSES:
    DRAFT     — being prepared
    SENT      — given/sent to customer
    ACCEPTED  — customer approved, ready to invoice
    INVOICED  — converted to a sale
    EXPIRED   — validity period passed, not accepted
    REJECTED  — customer declined

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As an OWNER/CASHIER, I want to create a quote for a customer listing items and
  prices so they can review and approve before we proceed with the sale.

  As an OWNER, when a customer approves a quote, I want to convert it to a sale
  with one click without re-entering all the items.

  DATABASE TABLES NEEDED
  ----------------------
  quotations:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    customer_id     BIGINT REFERENCES customers(id)
    quote_number    TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE
    status          TEXT CHECK (status IN 'DRAFT','SENT','ACCEPTED','INVOICED','EXPIRED','REJECTED')
    valid_until     DATE
    discount_amount NUMERIC(12,2) DEFAULT 0
    total_amount    NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL
    notes           TEXT
    created_by      UUID REFERENCES users(id)
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()

  quotation_items:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    quote_id        BIGINT REFERENCES quotations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
    product_id      BIGINT REFERENCES products(id)
    quantity        NUMERIC(10,3) NOT NULL
    unit_price      NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL
    total_price     NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - /quotations                 — list with status filter and search
  - /quotations/new             — create quote form (same UX as POS)
  - /quotations/[id]            — view quote, change status, convert to sale
  - PDF: Quotation document (professional format with validity date)

  CONVERT TO SALE LOGIC
  ---------------------
  On [Convert to Sale] button:
    1. Create a new sale record from the quotation total
    2. Create sale_items from quotation_items
    3. Set quote status = 'INVOICED', store resulting sale_id on quotation
    4. Redirect to the created sale detail page

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] Quote can be created for walk-in or registered customer
  [ ] Quote PDF is professional with shop details, validity date, terms
  [ ] Quote status can be updated manually at any stage
  [ ] [Convert to Sale] button appears when status = ACCEPTED
  [ ] Converted sale deducts stock and creates audit log entry
  [ ] Quote shows linked sale reference after conversion
  [ ] Expired quotes (past valid_until) shown with EXPIRED badge
  [ ] OWNER, ADMIN, and CASHIER can create quotes


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P1-10]  PHYSICAL STOCKTAKE MODULE
  Priority : CRITICAL | Effort : XL | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  Every 3–6 months, a hardware shop must physically count all stock and reconcile
  with the system. Without a formal stocktake module, the process is chaotic —
  staff count on paper, owner manually adjusts each product one by one, and there
  is no audit trail showing what was found vs what was expected. System stock
  figures drift further from reality over time.

  WORKFLOW
  --------
  START SESSION → ASSIGN COUNTERS → COUNT BY CATEGORY → REVIEW VARIANCES → APPROVE

  STOCKTAKE STATUSES:
    IN_PROGRESS  — counting is underway, stock figures are frozen for reading
    REVIEWING    — counting complete, owner is reviewing variances
    APPROVED     — approved, all variances auto-adjusted
    CANCELLED    — session abandoned

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As an OWNER, I want to start a stocktake session that freezes system stock
  figures so I can compare them to a physical count.

  As a STORE_KEEPER, I want to enter the physical count for each product and see
  the difference from the system quantity instantly.

  As an OWNER, I want to review all variances before approving, and provide a
  reason for each adjustment.

  DATABASE TABLES NEEDED
  ----------------------
  stocktake_sessions:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    session_number  TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE
    status          TEXT CHECK (IN 'IN_PROGRESS','REVIEWING','APPROVED','CANCELLED')
    started_by      UUID REFERENCES users(id)
    approved_by     UUID REFERENCES users(id)
    notes           TEXT
    started_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
    completed_at    TIMESTAMPTZ

  stocktake_items:
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
    session_id      BIGINT REFERENCES stocktake_sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
    product_id      BIGINT REFERENCES products(id)
    system_qty      NUMERIC(10,3) NOT NULL   -- frozen at session start
    counted_qty     NUMERIC(10,3)            -- entered by staff
    variance        NUMERIC(10,3)            -- counted - system
    variance_reason TEXT
    counted_by      UUID REFERENCES users(id)
    counted_at      TIMESTAMPTZ

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
