────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P2-10]  WHATSAPP / EMAIL RECEIPT DELIVERY
  Priority : IMPORTANT | Effort : M | Dependency : None
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  Many customers, especially construction companies and trade businesses, prefer
  a digital receipt via WhatsApp rather than a printed paper. In Sri Lanka,
  WhatsApp is the primary business communication channel. Digital receipts also
  reduce paper costs and are easier for customers to file.

  USER STORIES
  ------------
  As a CASHIER, after completing a sale, I want to send the receipt to the
  customer's WhatsApp so they have a digital copy without needing to print.

  IMPLEMENTATION APPROACH
  -----------------------
  WhatsApp: Use WhatsApp Business API (Meta Cloud API) or wa.me deep link.
    - Simple approach: Generate a pre-filled wa.me link with receipt summary text
    - Advanced: WhatsApp Business API to send PDF attachment directly
    - Simple approach requires no API key — works via browser opening WhatsApp Web

  Email: Use Resend API (or Supabase email) to send receipt PDF as attachment.

  SCREENS NEEDED
  --------------
  - After sale completion modal: [Send WhatsApp] and [Send Email] buttons
  - WhatsApp button: opens wa.me/94XXXXXXXXX link with pre-filled message
  - Email button: input field for email, [Send] fires server action
  - Success toast: "Receipt sent to 077XXXXXXX"

  WHATSAPP SIMPLE APPROACH (no API key needed)
  --------------------------------------------
  const message = `Receipt from [Shop Name]\nSale #${saleId}\nTotal: Rs.${total}\nDate: ${date}`
  const url = `https://wa.me/94${phone}?text=${encodeURIComponent(message)}`
  window.open(url, '_blank')
  This opens WhatsApp Web/App with the pre-filled message — cashier hits Send.

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] WhatsApp button appears on sale completion screen
  [ ] Clicking WhatsApp opens pre-filled message with key sale details
  [ ] Email sends receipt PDF as attachment to customer email
  [ ] Phone/email pre-filled from customer record if customer is registered
  [ ] Both options work for walk-in (manual phone entry) and registered customers


