────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [P3-08]  OFFLINE MODE / PROGRESSIVE WEB APP (PWA)
  Priority : ADVANCED | Effort : XXL | Dependency : ALL features
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  BUSINESS CONTEXT
  ----------------
  The system is fully cloud-based. In Sri Lanka, internet disruptions are common.
  If the internet goes down, the shop cannot process any sales. An offline-capable
  system that syncs when connectivity returns would make the system much more
  resilient.

  TECHNICAL APPROACH
  ------------------
  - Register a Service Worker to cache the app shell
  - Use IndexedDB to store pending sales when offline
  - On reconnect, sync pending sales to Supabase
  - Read-only data (product list) cached locally and refreshed when online

  COMPLEXITY WARNING
  ------------------
  This is the most technically complex feature in the entire roadmap. It requires:
  - Conflict resolution (what if stock was sold at both locations when offline?)
  - Queue management for pending operations
  - UI indicators for offline/online state and sync status
  - Testing across browser cache scenarios

  Recommended only after the system has been deployed and used live for at least
  6 months, and only if internet disruption is a genuine daily problem for clients.

  ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  -------------------
  [ ] POS screen is usable with no internet connection
  [ ] Offline sales are queued locally and synced when connection returns
  [ ] Clear indicator shown when system is in offline mode
  [ ] Sync conflict handled gracefully (not silently ignored)


